         <div type="bio">
            <p>German singer and translator. Mettal lived in Zurich during and after WWI. She translated JJ’s <name type="work" key="W_EXILES">Exiles</name> as <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Verbannte</name> (Zurich: Rascher, 1919). While living in Zurich, she gave several poetry recitations at the Tonhalle and the Kaufleuten theaters. In 1925 she wrote to Sylvia Beach proposing that she translate <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name>, but the project never materialized (Andreas Fischer, <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">James Joyce in Zurich: A Guide</name> [Cham: Palgrave Macmillan, 2020]). <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
